WEBVTT

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.280
Good morning, Jeff.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.080
Good morning, Arthur.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:17.600
Good morning, Kate.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.190
Good morning, everyone.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.170
<i>Vash, come back immediately!</i>

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.440
<i>This is a Level E-3 emergency.</i>

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:42.960
<i>Formation maintenance program: 
phase 5 recalculating. </i>

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.170
<i>This ship is in free fall.</i>

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.480
<i>Please evacuate as quickly as possible. </i>

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:52.350
<i>Once again, please evacuate 
as quickly as possible.</i>

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.080
She's not here!

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:56.790
Vash!

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.160
Nai! Rem!

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:04.940
What's going on?!
Why is the ship in free fall?!

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:08.640
Everything's fine. 
The ship's AI is just exaggerating.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.990
Now follow me, you two.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.080
Get inside. And hurry.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.680
What about everyone still sleeping?

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.550
They'll be able to escape, right?

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.590
Of course they will.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.100
Now get ready.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.430
You come too, Rem.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:41.710
I love you both.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.310
Rem?

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:48.940
Vash, Nai... I want you two to survive.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:51.520
Meeting you...

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.540
...has brought me so much joy!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.760
R-Rem!

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.060
REM!

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.190
<i>The time is now 10:00 AM 
on the morning of May 25th.</i>

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:18.030
<i>This is November Public
Broadcasting's satellite news,</i>

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.890
<i>where we bring you the
latest news from all regions.</i>

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:26.130
<i>The JuLai government has announced 
a new Most Wanted fugitive.</i>

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.640
JuLai doesn't do that often.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.440
Man, what a waste.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:32.000
<i>He is considered a person of interest 
in a series of mass murders.</i>

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.110
You tryin' to die young, newbie?

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:34.240
You shouldn't be drinking while
we're working anyway, Roberto.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.280
<i>Any cities with information 
are asked to reach out.</i>

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.360
Moreover...

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.160
My name is <i>not</i> "newbie."

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.710
Thanks for the update.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.940
Graduated from November University, huh?

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.230
Pretty elite.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.740
Becoming a reporter was my dream.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:53.600
Not much of a dream.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.120
Someday I'll be on the news desk—

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:00.950
Wow, I didn't know we had a rising
star on this little gossip piece.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.150
This is why I didn't want
to babysit a newbie.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:10.280
We're on the job.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.550
Also, please refer to me by my name.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:15.040
I'm Meryl Stryfe.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.760
That so?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.810
Well, let me tell you something, newbie.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.440
This scorching planet, Noman's Land,

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.280
is cruel beyond belief.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.530
It's a dog-eat-dog world.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.080
You'll find out soon enough.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:44.430
You've got a lot to learn about doing 
what it takes to survive, young lady.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.510
Are you done mocking me?

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.440
You're spilling my booze!

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.950
Just you wait until I get my big scoop...

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.450
Right, sure.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.910
I'll be running the news bureau!

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.320
Calm down, would you?

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.020
Are you listening?

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.280
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.800
I forgot to charge the battery...

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:12.700
You'll be toast before you know it.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.260
I'm thirsty...

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:26.260
Does that "Humanoid Typhoon" 
or whatever even exist?

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.670
You've seriously never heard of him?

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:32.270
If you meet him, you're done for.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:35.470
He's a walking disaster.

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.890
That's how he got that nickname...

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.380
The Humanoid Typhoon.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:45.790
Real people aren't monsters like that.
There's no way.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:49.170
But I won't give up, no matter how 
unreasonable the assignment!

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:49.860
Sure.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.060
No matter how long it takes, 
I'll get my scoop—

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:55.820
Roberto!

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.350
That'd be the aftermath.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.970
Looks like the work of the Bad Lads Gang.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:08.340
They really did a number on this corpse.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:20.880
There it goes.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.020
Creepy...

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.740
I agree. Let's go.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.470
Hey, hold on!

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:38.310
But...

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.200
We can't just leave him hanging here.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:42.790
Hey...

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.660
Thank you.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:50.570
Are you a gunman?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:55.470
Yeah, I guess... 
But I'm not much of a fighter.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:57.400
A gunman who's not a fighter?

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.400
Lost technology, eh?

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.140
I recognize those uniforms.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:10.600
What are the JuLai military police 
doing all the way out here?

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:11.640
Military police?

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.850
They can help us!

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.700
Hey!

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.010
Over here!

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.520
Good, a person.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.320
Have you seen this man around here?

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:27.600
Well? Have you, young lady?

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:30.630
What has this man done?

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.850
Reporters, eh?

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:33.890
You must have heard of him, then.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:36.190
They call him the Humanoid Typhoon.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:39.700
He's killed folks all over,
and he's running around destroying plants.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:42.260
He's a vicious criminal with a
$$6,000,000 bounty on his head.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.740
So, have you seen him or not?

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.040
I saw him!

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:50.430
Over there!

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:51.790
He went that way!

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.600
You should have said so sooner, fool!

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.810
Thank you!

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.650
I'll turn you over to the military police 
<i>after</i> I get an exclusive interview!

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.190
Well done, newbie.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.860
My name's Meryl Stryfe.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.210
And besides, if he's been falsely accused,

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.230
it's our job as reporters to clear his name.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.520
Running into such nice folks...
I can't believe my luck!

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.580
What a blessing!

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:21.410
Oh, don't go flattering me.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:23.240
There's something sketchy about him.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:28.600
Why don't we do the exclusive interview 
at the diner instead of out here?

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.220
What?

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:30.080
Huh?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.090
There's a diner?

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:31.710
Yeah?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.210
Wh-Why didn't you say so earlier?!

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.030
Is it this way?

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.530
W-W-W-W-Wait! Not that way!

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.170
So is it this way?

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:40.260
Er, no...

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.150
Then it has to be this way!

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.940
No, not exactly...

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:44.880
The Humanoid Typhoon, huh?

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.230
Is there really a diner?

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:48.490
Vash the Stampede.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:47.860
Yes...

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.860
Then tell me where it is!

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.100
Just who is he?

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.420
Damn it!

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:03.110
Water...

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:11.180
The western city of Jeneora Rock.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:29.740
Oh my.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:35.400
This ain't a place for kids, little miss!

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.440
Water, please.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.020
I can't hear you if you don't speak up.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.010
I figured she'd be here!

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:45.640
This newbie's more trouble than most.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:48.680
Vash!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.340
Got a second on the way, Rosa?

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:52.170
Looks like it.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:52.830
Where's the hubby?

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.630
I kicked his lazy ass out.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:55.980
You never change.

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.060
You two seem pretty close...

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:01.960
He saved the whole town
 of Jeneora Rock, after all.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:02.870
He did?

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.800
And just who are you, exactly?

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.570
What are you planning to do with Vash?

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:08.800
Depending on your answer, 
things might get bloody.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.370
They're both friends of mine!

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.230
Then what's with the rope around you?

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.430
What rope?

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:16.850
Fine.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.620
You must have a good reason 
for being with them.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:23.080
What'll it be for the lot of you?

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:24.250
I'll have a whiskey.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.690
We're on the job.

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:26.850
Three waters, please.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:29.730
Graduates are so uptight.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.830
I'll have you know that's what got me
 good grades at November University...

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:36.540
Newbie...

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:45.300
Sorry it's dirty.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:47.800
Our water-producing plant broke down,

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:50.430
so we've been buying it from another town.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:53.450
No one will have clean water for a while.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:54.510
Your plant?

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:59.430
But since you three came around, 
maybe things are looking up for us.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:03.300
Would you take another look at it, Vash?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.370
Wouldn't have pegged you
as a plant engineer.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.490
I know, right?

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:25.120
It broke down a few years ago as well.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.630
Vash fixed it, free of charge.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.650
So that's how he saved the town.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.630
You know what plants are, I trust, newbie.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:36.900
Of course I do!

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:39.100
They're biological generators

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:43.580
that produce everything humanity needs 
to survive on this desert planet.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.370
Part of the technology lost
 after the Spacefaring Age.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:50.340
A textbook answer from Miss Good Grades.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:53.970
We can't build them anymore.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:59.030
If you want one, you have 
to pay a premium or steal it.

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:02.150
Hence why every town 
keeps tight control of theirs.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.800
That one's red...

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.520
A red plant...

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.220
Is that bad?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.410
It's dying.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:14.330
What?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.730
Buying a new one would cost a fortune.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:23.780
But if we do nothing, 
something even worse will happen.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.650
So you need a ton of money, do you?

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:31.370
We've tracked you down, Humanoid Typhoon!

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:33.330
The JuLai military police?

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:38.120
Haven't you heard about the huge 
bounty on that man's head?

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.210
Six million...?

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:46.820
Funnily enough, that's just
about the cost of a new plant.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:51.230
If you turn him in,
 it'll solve this town's problems.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:53.760
I'd really prefer not to fight...

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:57.000
Then come along quietly!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.160
Tie him up!

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:09.500
This is awful...

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:12.240
No one's gonna save you!

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:16.290
Six million is worth more 
to them than your life!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:20.210
Ow... Maybe we could
settle this peacefully?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.250
Okay, let's take him back to JuLai.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.440
What an easy job.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.510
On your feet!

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:29.770
Hey, hey, hey now!
You sure about this?

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:32.510
Roberto?

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.730
This is gonna make a great article.

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.540
You're the reporter from the desert.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.680
How about this for a headline?

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:42.650
"JuLai Military Police Show Their Weakness,

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:47.300
Cowardly Drawing Guns on Unarmed Suspect!"

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.120
What? Oh... Right!

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:54.050
If you're a real man, 
you'll settle this with a duel.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:54.830
A duel?!

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.530
Great idea!

00:14:55.530 --> 00:15:01.620
Otherwise you'll be known as a 
coward for the rest of your days.

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:03.760
Enough!

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.860
It was a joke! We were just kidding!

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.490
You're on.

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.390
Captain!

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:09.170
Are you serious?

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.140
A duel?

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:14.220
Um...

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.880
It's a duel!

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:17.890
I've got 5,000 on Vash!

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.480
I'm putting 10,000 on the JuLai guy!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:24.940
This will be a quick-draw duel! 
The last man standing wins!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.740
Roberto, I'm not sure a duel 
was the best idea...

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:33.880
I mean, he seems <i>really</i> bad at this.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:37.190
You don't win a duel by drawing first.

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:37.900
Huh?

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:41.630
If you shoot too early or too slow, you lose.

00:15:41.630 --> 00:15:43.520
Just watch.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.710
He might not be as bad as you think.

00:15:57.340 --> 00:15:58.220
Draw.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:02.370
Draw!

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:03.930
No.

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:06.450
Draw! This is a duel!

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:08.640
I said no.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.980
This is stupid.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.850
I suppose you're right.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.160
It <i>is</i> stupid.

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:37.210
A fight should be a show!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.340
Captain!

00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:45.610
Firing a cluster bomb 
will put us all in danger!

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:48.650
We're supposed to capture 
him alive, Captain!

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.660
R-Run!

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:57.310
I never wanted to duel you 
in the first place!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:59.910
Let's enjoy ourselves, Humanoid Typhoon!

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.910
He's crazy...

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.430
That coward!

00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:08.330
You've nearly died enough today, newbie.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.570
Remember, we're only reporters.

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:14.130
We're not military police or bodyguards.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:14.760
But...

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:21.670
You'd do well to remember only the privileged
 get to sling around the word "coward."

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.620
Got that?

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:25.890
Yes.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:28.270
Vash, this way! Hurry!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.650
Take cover inside!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.900
He's trying to keep everyone 
out of harm's way.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.760
Acting brave now is pretty foolish.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.700
He's like you: not long for this world.

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.840
Huh...? Wait, what? Huh?

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.910
What...? What? Wh-What?!

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:59.660
Huh?! H-H-H-H-Huh?!

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:00.630
How the...

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:01.880
Don't tell me...

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:05.020
Um, I'm out of bullets.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:05.850
Unbelievable.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:09.870
What an idiot!

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:12.320
Ammo! Please, I need some ammo!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:15.290
Does anyone have .22 caliber bullets?!

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.400
Someone!

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:20.650
Anyone!

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.630
Why isn't anyone helping him?

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.040
Huh?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:34.690
Please! I need .22 caliber bullets!

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.380
I've got one!

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.420
This is from Rosa!

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:47.920
Huh?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:49.850
Hey!

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:51.850
My bullet!

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:05.950
Gotcha!

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.690
Just one bullet?

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.240
Not my fault.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:10.470
Thank you.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:16.630
I don't think so!

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:20.080
That's enough!

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.570
Y-You'll pay for this!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:05.160
You sure know how to handle a gun.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:11.140
Gosh, that sure was a surprise!
 I wasn't sure one bullet would be enough.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:15.100
I'm one lucky duck.

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:21.400
Who are you afraid of?

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:24.880
Does it have something 
to do with that red plant?

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:31.840
You weren't fazed in the least 
by the military police.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:37.410
So tell me... What <i>does</i> scare you?

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:40.790
I have a brother.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:55.800
A brilliant success! I finally did it!

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.810
How could you?

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:02.530
Don't worry. I made sure 
the plant ship would survive.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.490
But you killed even <i>Rem</i>!

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.030
Don't you scold me.

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:09.700
You're my accomplice.

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:24.130
Right, Vash?

00:21:43.440 --> 00:21:45.150
Millions Knives.

00:21:45.920 --> 00:21:48.660
Have you ever heard that name?

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:54.620
So you've found him.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.540
Take me there to retrieve him.

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:03.390
They're filthy parasites...

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:11.170
And this time, I'll completely eliminate them.
